-- title:
--   Atom-union membership is determined by the canonical atom
-- statement:
--   Let $\Omega$ be finite, let $P$ be a face partition of $\Omega$, and let $s$ be a finite collection of its atoms. For any $x\in\Omega$, let $a_P(x)$ be its canonical partition atom. Then
--   $$
--   x\in\bigcup_{a\in s}a\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad a_P(x)\in s.
--   $$
--   The statement expresses membership in an atom union using the unique atom containing the point.
